        # --- Clay Millennium Problems (remaining) ---
        _sd("Poincaré Conjecture Revisited: 4D Smooth", "The 3D Poincaré conjecture is proven, but the smooth 4D version remains open: does every smooth 4-manifold homotopy equivalent to S⁴ necessarily diffeomorphic to S⁴? Formalize Donaldson's invariants, Seiberg-Witten theory, and explore exotic smooth structures on 4-manifolds.", ["Geometry", "Topology"], 0.95),
        _sd("Riemann Hypothesis: Zero-Free Regions", "Prove that a positive proportion of zeros of the Riemann zeta function lie on the critical line. Formalize Selberg's result (positive proportion on), Conrey's 2/5 result, and explore connections to random matrix theory and the moment problem.", ["NumberTheory", "Analysis"], 0.93),
        _sd("BSD Conjecture: Rank Computability", "Prove that the rank of an elliptic curve over Q is computable. Formalize the Mordell-Weil theorem, height pairings, and descent algorithms. Connect to the conjecture that ranks are bounded and explore the parity conjecture.", ["Algebra", "NumberTheory"], 0.92),
        _sd("Catalan's Conjecture Generalizations", "Mihailescu proved that 8 and 9 are the only consecutive perfect powers. Generalize: find all solutions to x^a - y^b = k for fixed small k. Formalize the theory of exponential Diophantine equations and Pillai's conjecture.", ["NumberTheory", "Algebra"], 0.88),
        _sd("Brocard's Problem: n! + 1 = m²", "Determine all integer solutions to n! + 1 = m². Only three solutions are known (n=4,5,7). Formalize the connection to the ABC conjecture and explore bounds on the spacing between Brown numbers.", ["NumberTheory"], 0.82),
        _sd("Wall-Sun-Sun Primes", "Prove that Wall-Sun-Sun primes exist (primes p where p² divides F_{p-(p|5)}). Formalize the connection to Fermat's Last Theorem and establish search bounds for the first such prime.", ["NumberTheory", "Algebra"], 0.84),
        _sd("Sierpiński Numbers: Covering Systems", "Prove that 78557 is the smallest Sierpiński number. Formalize the theory of covering systems and their relationship to Chinese Remainder Theorem configurations.", ["NumberTheory", "Computation"], 0.86),
        _sd("Legendre's Three-Square Theorem Extension", "Characterize numbers representable as a sum of three squares of primes. Formalize the circle method approach to ternary Goldbach-type problems for squares.", ["NumberTheory"], 0.80),
        _sd("Artin's Conjecture on Primitive Roots", "Prove that any integer a ≠ -1,□ that is not a perfect square is a primitive root modulo infinitely many primes. Formalize the Hooley conditional proof under GRH and explore unconditional density results.", ["NumberTheory", "Algebra"], 0.89),
        _sd("Hadwiger's Conjecture", "Prove that every loopless graph requiring k+1 colors for a proper coloring contains K_{k+1} as a minor. Formalize known cases (k ≤ 5), the Wagner equivalence, and the connection to the Four Color Theorem.", ["Combinatorics", "Geometry"], 0.90),
        _sd("Erdős-Faber-Lovász Conjecture", "Prove that the union of k k-uniform intersecting hypergraphs has chromatic number at most k. Formalize the linear hypergraph version and recent probabilistic approaches.", ["Combinatorics"], 0.83),
        _sd("Sensitivity Conjecture Extensions", "Huang proved the sensitivity conjecture. Extend: prove tighter bounds on degree-sensitivity relationship of Boolean functions. Formalize the spectral approach via signed adjacency matrices.", ["Computation", "Algebra"], 0.81),
        _sd("Graceful Tree Conjecture", "Prove that every tree admits a graceful labeling. Formalize known results for paths, caterpillars, and olive trees. Explore connections to decompositions of complete graphs.", ["Combinatorics", "Algebra"], 0.79),
        _sd("Reconstruction Conjecture", "Prove that every graph on at least 3 vertices is determined up to isomorphism by its deck of vertex-deleted subgraphs. Formalize Kelly's lemma and prove for specific graph classes.", ["Combinatorics", "Logic"], 0.82),
        _sd("Rota's Basis Conjecture", "Prove that for n bases of an n-dimensional vector space, there is a way to arrange all n² elements into an n×n grid so that each row and column is a basis.", ["Algebra", "Combinatorics"], 0.84),
        _sd("Jacobian Conjecture", "Prove that every polynomial map F: Cⁿ → Cⁿ with Jacobian determinant 1 has a polynomial inverse. Formalize known reductions (degree 3 suffices) and connections to Dixmier and Kellers problems.", ["Algebra", "Geometry"], 0.88),
        _sd("Kaplansky's Conjectures", "Resolve Kaplansky's conjectures on group rings: no zero divisors, no idempotents other than 0/1, and no nontrivial units in K[G] for torsion-free G.", ["Algebra", "Computation"], 0.85),
        _sd("Bourgain's Slicing Problem", "Prove that every convex body K in Rⁿ of volume 1 has a hyperplane section of (n-1)-dimensional volume at least c for some universal c > 0.", ["Geometry", "Analysis"], 0.83),
        _sd("Sendov's Conjecture", "Prove that for every polynomial with all roots in the closed unit disk, every root has a critical point within distance 1 of it. Formalize known partial results and the connection to Gauss-Lucas.", ["Analysis", "Algebra"], 0.80),
        _sd("Standard Conjectures on Algebraic Cycles", "Prove Grothendieck's standard conjectures: numerical and homological equivalence coincide, Künneth projectors are algebraic, and independence of l. Connect to the Hodge conjecture and motives.", ["Geometry", "Algebra"], 0.91),
        _sd("Resolution of Singularities in Positive Characteristic", "Prove Hironaka's resolution of singularities theorem for varieties in characteristic p > 0. Formalize known results for dimensions ≤ 3.", ["Geometry", "Algebra"], 0.89),
        _sd("Novikov Conjecture", "Prove that higher signatures are homotopy invariants for all finitely presented groups. Formalize the assembly map in topological K-theory and connections to Baum-Connes.", ["Geometry", "Topology"], 0.87),
        _sd("Baum-Connes Conjecture", "Prove the Baum-Connes conjecture relating K-theory of reduced C*-algebras to equivariant K-homology. Formalize known cases and the connection to Novikov.", ["Algebra", "Geometry"], 0.90),
        _sd("Self-Avoiding Walk: Connective Constant", "Prove that the connective constant for the self-avoiding walk on Z² equals (2+√2)/2 or determine its exact value. Formalize the Hara-Slade result and Nienhuis's conjecture.", ["Probability", "Combinatorics"], 0.84),
        _sd("Normality of Mathematical Constants", "Prove that π, e, √2, or any fundamental constant is normal. Formalize the connection to equidistribution and algebraic independence.", ["NumberTheory", "Probability"], 0.81),
        _sd("Random Matrices: Edge Universality", "Prove edge universality for random matrix ensembles beyond Gaussian cases. Formalize Tracy-Widom distribution convergence and the Airy kernel.", ["Probability", "Algebra"], 0.85),
        _sd("One-Way Functions: Existence and Hierarchy", "Formalize the lattice of cryptographic hardness assumptions: one-way functions → pseudorandom generators → pseudorandom functions → secure encryption. Prove separation results.", ["Cryptography", "Computation"], 0.90),
        _sd("Learning with Errors: Hardness Reductions", "Formalize the hardness reduction from worst-case lattice problems (GapSVP, SIVP) to the Learning with Errors problem with specific parameters.", ["Cryptography", "Computation"], 0.88),
        _sd("Isogeny-Based Cryptography: CSI-FiSh", "Formalize the class group action on isogeny graphs of elliptic curves. Prove that CSIDH is a one-way function assuming hardness of computing isogenies.", ["Cryptography", "Algebra"], 0.86),
        _sd("Natural Proofs Barrier: Formalization", "Formalize the Razborov-Rudich natural proofs barrier: circuit lower bound proofs using 'natural' properties cannot separate P from NP unless pseudorandom generators don't exist. Explore algebrization.", ["Computation", "Logic"], 0.94),
        _sd("Unique Games Conjecture", "Prove or disprove: for every ε > 0, there exists k such that distinguishing value ≥ 1-ε from value ≤ ε for unique 2-prover games with k labels is NP-hard. Connect to MAX-CUT and SDP gaps.", ["Computation", "Logic"], 0.92),
        _sd("Whitehead Problem: Independence from ZFC", "Prove that the Whitehead problem (every Whitehead group is free) is independent of ZFC. Formalize Shelah's undecidability proof: consistent both ways.", ["Algebra", "Logic"], 0.91),
        _sd("Large Cardinal Hierarchy: Consistency Strength", "Formalize the consistency strength hierarchy: inaccessible < Mahlo < measurable < strong < supercompact < huge. Prove strictness results.", ["Logic", "SetTheory"], 0.89),
        _sd("Vaught's Conjecture", "Prove that for any countable first-order theory, the number of countable models is either countable or 2^ℵ₀. Formalize Morley's theorem and the topological version.", ["Logic"], 0.83),
        _sd("Reverse Mathematics: Ramsey's Theorem", "Classify RT²₂ in the reverse mathematics hierarchy: prove it's strictly between ACA₀ and WKL₀ over RCA₀. Formalize Seetapun's theorem.", ["Logic", "Computation"], 0.85),
        _sd("Yamabe Problem: Non-Compact Case", "Prove the Yamabe problem on non-compact Riemannian manifolds: find a conformal metric of constant scalar curvature. Formalize the compact case and explore non-compact obstructions.", ["Geometry", "Analysis"], 0.86),
        _sd("Willmore Conjecture Generalizations", "Prove sharp lower bounds for the Willmore energy of surfaces by genus. Extend the Marques-Neves proof for tori to higher-genus surfaces.", ["Geometry"], 0.82),
        _sd("Kähler-Einstein Metrics and K-Stability", "Formalize the Yau-Tian-Donaldson conjecture: a Fano manifold admits a Kähler-Einstein metric iff it is K-stable. Prove stability criteria for specific Fano varieties.", ["Geometry", "Algebra"], 0.88),
        _sd("Yang-Mills Mass Gap", "Prove that quantum Yang-Mills theory on R⁴ exists as a rigorous QFT with a mass gap. Formalize lattice gauge theory and the Clay Millennium formulation.", ["Physics", "Analysis"], 0.95),
        _sd("Tropical Fermat's Last Theorem", "Characterize solutions to x⊕y = z in the tropical semiring. Formalize tropical varieties and prove a Kapranov-type theorem for tropical Fermat curves.", ["Tropical", "Algebra"], 0.83),
        _sd("Tropical Hodge Theory", "Prove a tropical analog of the Hodge decomposition. Formalize tropical (p,q)-forms, the tropical Laplacian, and harmonic theory on balanced weighted polyhedral complexes.", ["Tropical", "Geometry"], 0.86),
        _sd("Idempotent Probability: Large Deviations", "Develop a large deviation principle for max-plus probability measures. Prove that max-plus random walks satisfy an LDP with rate function given by the Legendre-Fenchel transform.", ["Tropical", "Probability"], 0.81),
        _sd("Neural Tangent Kernel: Convergence", "Prove that neural networks in the lazy regime converge to the NTK solution. Formalize the Jacot-Gabriel-Hongler theorem and prove universality across architectures.", ["MachineLearning", "Analysis"], 0.84),
        _sd("Grokking: Phase Transitions in Learning", "Formalize grokking: prove a delayed generalization theorem for two-layer networks and characterize the phase transition as a saddle-node bifurcation.", ["MachineLearning", "Physics"], 0.80),
        _sd("Scaling Laws from Statistical Mechanics", "Prove neural network scaling laws from first principles. Derive power-law relationships between loss, model size, dataset size, and compute from the GP kernel spectrum.", ["MachineLearning", "Physics"], 0.82),
        _sd("Langlands for GL₂ over Q", "Prove the Langlands correspondence for GL₂ over Q: every algebraic automorphic representation corresponds to a Galois representation. Formalize Eichler-Shimura and Deligne cases.", ["Bridges", "Algebra"], 0.96),
        _sd("Arithmetic Mirror Symmetry for Calabi-Yau", "Prove arithmetic mirror symmetry: the number of rational curves on X equals the rank of the Picard group of its mirror Y. Formalize the SYZ picture and modularity of CY zeta functions.", ["Bridges", "Geometry"], 0.91),
        _sd("Topological Quantum Computing: Braiding Universality", "Prove that any quantum circuit can be approximated by braiding anyons. Formalize the Jones polynomial as a universal topological quantum invariant and prove density in SU(2).", ["Bridges", "Physics"], 0.89),
        _sd("Entropy Power Inequality: Sharp Version", "Prove the sharp entropy power inequality for all dimensions with equality conditions. Connect to the Brunn-Minkowski inequality and prove stability versions.", ["Bridges", "Probability"], 0.83),
        _sd("Homotopy Type Theory as Foundations", "Prove that univalent foundations (HoTT) provide a consistent alternative to ZFC. Formalize the univalence axiom, compute homotopy groups of spheres, and establish constructive interpretability.", ["Bridges", "Logic"], 0.87),
        _sd("p-adic Langlands for GL₂(Q_p)", "Formalize the p-adic Langlands correspondence for GL₂(Q_p): establish a bijection between irreducible unitary Banach representations and 2-dimensional Galois representations. Prove the Colmez functor realization.", ["Bridges", "NumberTheory"], 0.93),

        # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        # Wave 7: Moonshots, Sci-Fi, Black Mirror, Rucker-esque Wild
        # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

        # --- Consciousness & Strange Loops (Hofstadter) ---
        _sd("Strange Loops: Self-Reference and Gödel's Incompleteness", "Prove that any sufficiently powerful formal system necessarily contains strange loops: statements that refer to their own unprovability. Formalize Gödel's first incompleteness theorem as a fixed-point in the lattice of provability predicates. Explore whether consciousness arises from tangled hierarchies of self-referential symbols.", ["Novelty", "Logic", "Computation"], 0.90),
        _sd("Isomorphisms of Meaning: When Structures Collide", "Prove that isomorphic mathematical structures can carry semantically different meanings that no formal system can distinguish. Formalize the concept of 'isomorphism of isomorphisms' and show that categorical equivalence preserves truth but not meaning. Connect to Hofstadter's Copycat architecture for analogical reasoning.", ["Novelty", "Logic", "Algebra"], 0.85),
        _sd("Tangled Hierarchies: Proof Systems That Reference Their Own Soundness", "Construct a formal proof system where the soundness predicate appears inside the system it validates. Prove that such tangled hierarchies are unavoidable in any system that can reason about its own consistency. Formalize using modal fixed-point logics and Kripke frames.", ["Novelty", "Logic", "Computation"], 0.88),
        _sd("Consciousness as Emergent Fixed Point", "Formalize the hypothesis that consciousness is a fixed point of a self-modeling function: a system that models itself modeling itself. Prove that such fixed points exist in sufficiently rich Cartesian closed categories and that they exhibit strange-loop topology. Connect to the Yoneda lemma and self-reference in type theory.", ["Novelty", "Logic", "Bridges"], 0.86),

        # --- Rudy Rucker: Infinity, Transreals, and Mind ---
        _sd("Transfinite Game Theory: Games That Last Forever", "Develop a rigorous theory of infinite games where moves are indexed by transfinite ordinals. Prove that Zermelo's theorem extends: every such game has a determined outcome under AD. Formalize the connection between the determinacy hierarchy and large cardinal axioms.", ["Novelty", "Logic", "SetTheory"], 0.87),
        _sd("Transreal Arithmetic: Computing Beyond Plus-Minus Infinity", "Formalize transreal arithmetic (Anderson's system: R ∪ {Phi, +inf, -inf} with Phi = 0/0). Prove the ring axioms fail but a wheel structure emerges. Determine which theorems of real analysis survive transreal extension and which collapse.", ["Novelty", "Algebra", "Computation"], 0.82),
        _sd("Infinite-Dimensional Chess: Winning on the Hilbert Board", "Formalize chess played on an infinite board. Prove that the king can always escape on an infinite board and determine which finite-piece configurations are forced mates. Develop a theory of infinite combinatorial game value and prove its relationship to ordinal game values.", ["Novelty", "Computation", "Logic"], 0.80),
        _sd("Cellular Automata at the Ordinals: Transfinite Computation", "Prove that cellular automata can perform transfinite computations when run on ordinals instead of N. Formalize a Rule 110 analog on omega-squared and prove it achieves super-Turing computation. Connect to Infinite Time Turing Machines and ordinal computation.", ["Novelty", "Computation", "Logic"], 0.84),
        _sd("Mind vs Gödel: Can Minds Outperform Algorithms?", "Formalize the Lucas-Penrose argument that human minds can see truths that formal systems cannot prove about themselves. Prove or disprove: there exists a computational system that can consistently recognize its own Gödel sentences. Connect to Chaitin's incompleteness theorem and the Berry paradox.", ["Novelty", "Logic", "Computation"], 0.89),

        # --- Black Mirror: Dystopian Math ---
        _sd("Social Credit Scores as Topological Invariants", "Formalize social credit systems as continuous maps from a population to a totally ordered set. Prove that any such map creates fixed-point attractors in the social graph topology. Show that under reasonable assumptions, credit scores converge to a Cantor set attractor where small perturbations cause phase transitions.", ["Novelty", "Bridges", "Computation"], 0.83),
        _sd("Surveillance Networks: Information-Theoretic Undetectability", "Prove a theorem about the minimum information an observer must collect to reconstruct a dynamic social network with bounded error. Formalize the privacy-utility tradeoff as a rate-distortion problem and prove that perfect surveillance and perfect privacy are mutually exclusive in finite networks.", ["Novelty", "Cryptography", "Bridges"], 0.86),
        _sd("Memory Editing: When Forgetting Is a Mathematical Operation", "Formalize memory as a monoid homomorphism from experience streams to compressed representations. Prove that any such homomorphism satisfying a finite-memory bound must be lossy and that the information loss forms a submonoid. Show that targeted forgetting is equivalent to a quotient construction in the category of memory algebras.", ["Novelty", "Algebra", "Computation"], 0.81),
        _sd("Digital Immortality: Can a Mind Be Encoded?", "Prove information-theoretic bounds on mind uploading: the minimum description length of a human mind exceeds any computable compression of its neural connectome. Formalize the Bekenstein bound applied to neural computation and show that the Kolmogorov complexity of consciousness is at least quadratic in synapse count.", ["Novelty", "Computation", "Physics"], 0.85),
        _sd("Self-Modifying Code That Cannot Be Stopped", "Prove that any Turing-complete system with self-modification capabilities has no general algorithm for predicting its own termination. Formalize the halting problem for programs that can rewrite their own code mid-execution and show this is strictly harder than the classical halting problem. Connect to the virus paradox and AI alignment.", ["Novelty", "Computation", "Logic"], 0.88),

        # --- Twilight Zone: Impossible Geometries ---
        _sd("Non-Desarguesian Worlds: Geometry Without Desargues", "Construct and classify finite projective planes where Desargues' theorem fails. Prove that such planes exist at every prime power order and that their collineation groups are strictly smaller than PGL. Formalize the connection to non-associative division algebras and Hall triple systems.", ["Novelty", "Geometry", "Algebra"], 0.84),
        _sd("Negative-Dimensional Topology: What Lives in Dimension -1?", "Develop a rigorous theory of negative-dimensional spaces using pro-spectra and formal dimension theory. Prove that Euler characteristic extends to negative dimensions and that chi(X) for dim X = -n satisfies chi = (-1)^n · |pi_0(X)|. Formalize the stabilization map from negative to positive dimensions.", ["Novelty", "Geometry", "Topology"], 0.83),
        _sd("The Topology of Impossible Objects: Escher Stairs and Klein Bottles", "Formalize the mathematical conditions under which impossible figures (Penrose triangles, Escher stairs) can exist as manifolds. Prove that every non-orientable 3-manifold contains an embedded Penrose triangle as a smoothly immersed surface. Classify which impossible figures are realizable as developable surfaces.", ["Novelty", "Geometry", "Topology"], 0.80),
        _sd("Time Travel Consistency: Novikov's Principle as a Fixed-Point Theorem", "Prove that Novikov's self-consistency principle follows from the Banach fixed-point theorem applied to the causal structure of spacetime. Formalize time-travel paradoxes as boundary value problems and prove existence of self-consistent solutions for polynomial causal maps.", ["Novelty", "Physics", "Bridges"], 0.87),
        _sd("Flatland Catastrophe: When 2D Physics Breaks", "Prove that 2-dimensional Newtonian gravity is mathematically pathological: orbits don't close, there's no stable circular orbit, and gravitational potential is logarithmic. Formalize the Bertrand-Darboux theorem failure in 2D and prove that stable planetary systems cannot exist in Flatland.", ["Novelty", "Physics", "Geometry"], 0.79),

        # --- Wild Explorations ---
        _sd("Dream Logic: Non-Monotone Reasoning Where Contradictions Coexist", "Formalize a logic where contradictions do not explode and beliefs can be retracted. Prove that paraconsistent logics can model dream-like reasoning where impossible objects coexist. Show that such logics correspond to topological spaces where open sets are not closed under arbitrary union.", ["Novelty", "Logic", "Computation"], 0.84),
        _sd("The Unreasonable Effectiveness of Wrong Theories", "Prove a meta-theorem: for any approximately correct physical theory T, there exists a class of phenomena for which T makes predictions closer to truth than any known correct theory. Formalize using perturbation theory on theory-space and prove that the wrongness of T forms a convergent series toward truth.", ["Novelty", "Physics", "Bridges"], 0.82),
        _sd("Surreal Topology: Open Sets at Infinity", "Extend topological space theory to include Conway's surreal numbers as the underlying set. Prove that the order topology on No is not first-countable and that every real open set has a surreal extension. Determine whether No is connected, compact, or paracompact in the interval topology.", ["Novelty", "Algebra", "Geometry"], 0.86),
        _sd("Anti-Mathematics: What If All Axioms Were Negated?", "Systematically negate the ZFC axioms and study the resulting anti-mathematics. Prove that not-Extensionality yields a theory of indistinguishable sets, not-Infinity yields hereditarily finite set theory, and not-Choice yields universes where every set is measurable. Determine which anti-axioms are consistent with each other.", ["Novelty", "Logic", "SetTheory"], 0.85),
        _sd("Thermodynamics of Mathematical Proof", "Formalize a Landauer-like principle for mathematical reasoning: every bit of information destroyed in a proof step costs at least kT ln 2 of entropy. Prove that there exist theorems whose shortest proof requires exponentially more erasure than creation, and connect to Kolmogorov complexity and the thermodynamic cost of verification.", ["Novelty", "Computation", "Physics"], 0.88),
        _sd("Hypercomputation: Computing the Uncomputable", "Construct a rigorous model of hypercomputation that can solve the halting problem. Prove that any physical system implementing hypercomputation requires infinite energy density or infinite precision. Formalize the distinction between accidentally computable (physical oracles) and essentially computable (Turing machines).", ["Novelty", "Computation", "Physics"], 0.87),
        _sd("Retrocausal Mathematics: Where Effects Precede Causes", "Formalize retrocausal mathematical structures where implications can flow backward in time. Prove that in a retrocausal Heyting algebra, the law of excluded middle fails but a temporal excluded middle holds. Connect to the CPT theorem in QFT and prove that any retrocausal logic must be intuitionistic.", ["Novelty", "Logic", "Physics"], 0.83),
        _sd("Computational Complexity of Alien Civilizations", "Prove that any technological civilization must discover computational complexity independently of its biological substrate. Formalize a universal complexity hierarchy and prove that P vs NP is a theorem about the structure of computation itself, not about any particular model. Show that even hypercomputational civilizations face analogous barriers.", ["Novelty", "Computation", "Logic"], 0.86),
        _sd("Paradoxes as Theorems: Liar, Berry, and Russell Made Consistent", "Construct a consistent formal system where the Liar sentence, Berry's paradox, and Russell's paradox are all provable theorems rather than contradictions. Prove this requires rejecting classical logic in favor of a paraconsistent logic with a nontrivial inconsistency-tolerant truth predicate. Show this system proves its own soundness.", ["Novelty", "Logic"], 0.84),
        _sd("Categorical Physics: The Shape of a Theory of Everything", "Prove that any theory of everything in physics must be a (2,infinity)-category with duals. Formalize the cobordism hypothesis as a universal property and show that TQFTs, CFTs, and string theories are all shadows of a single object in this higher category. Determine whether the resulting theory is computable or contains oracle information.", ["Novelty", "Physics", "Geometry"], 0.90),

        # --- Extra Wild ---
        _sd("Counterfactual Number Theory: What If Primes Were Random?", "Construct an alternate number theory where primes are replaced by a random subset of N with density n/log n. Prove which theorems survive (Dirichlet, PNT) and which collapse (unique factorization). Determine whether RH holds almost surely in this counterfactual universe.", ["Novelty", "NumberTheory", "Probability"], 0.85),
        _sd("Borges' Library of Babel: Combinatorics of Everything", "Compute the topological type of the Library of Babel: a space of all possible 410-page books. Prove that it is connected, totally disconnected under the Hamming metric, and has covering dimension 0. Determine the Kolmogorov complexity of a random book and prove that almost all books are incompressible.", ["Novelty", "Combinatorics", "Logic"], 0.81),
        _sd("Aleph-1 Surface: Geometry Between Dimensions", "Construct a surface whose Hausdorff dimension is exactly aleph-1 (assuming CH). Prove that such a surface cannot be embedded in any finite-dimensional Euclidean space but can be embedded in the Hilbert cube. Formalize transfinite-dimensional manifolds and prove they have no finite triangulation.", ["Novelty", "Geometry", "SetTheory"], 0.82),
        _sd("Reflective Type Theory: Proving Things About Proving Things", "Formalize a type theory where types can refer to their own provability. Prove that such a system can express 'this proposition is provable but not provably provable' as a well-typed term. Show that reflective type theory properly extends Martin-Lof type theory and that its proof term language is exactly the modal mu-calculus.", ["Novelty", "Logic", "Computation"], 0.86),
        _sd("Zombies and Qualia: Mathematics of Subjective Experience", "Formalize the hard problem of consciousness as a theorem about the gap between functional descriptions and subjective experience. Prove that any system satisfying the functional definition of consciousness can have a zombie twin that is functionally identical but experientially void. Show this gap is isomorphic to Gödel's incompleteness gap.", ["Novelty", "Logic", "Bridges"], 0.84),
        _sd("Fermat Near-Misses in the Twilight Zone", "Study near-misses to Fermat's Last Theorem: triples (a,b,c) where |a^n + b^n - c^n| is small. Prove that such near-misses exist for every n and characterize their distribution. Show that the density of near-misses decreases super-exponentially and connect to the ABC conjecture's effective version.", ["Novelty", "NumberTheory", "Algebra"], 0.83),
        _sd("The Fractal Dimension of Mathematical Truth", "Define a natural metric on the space of all mathematical statements and prove that the set of true statements has a fractal dimension. Show that this dimension is strictly between 0 and 1 (truth is sparse but not negligible). Connect to Chaitin's Omega and prove that the fractal dimension is uncomputable but approximable.", ["Novelty", "Logic", "Computation"], 0.87),
        _sd("Quantum Proofs of Classical Theorems", "Prove that every classical mathematical theorem has a quantum proof that is shorter by at most a polynomial factor. Formalize quantum proof systems (QMA) and show that some classical theorems (e.g., pigeonhole principle) have exponentially shorter quantum proofs. Determine whether super-polynomial quantum advantage exists.", ["Novelty", "Computation", "Physics"], 0.89),
        _sd("Aboriginal Kinship as Group Theory: Dreamtime Algebra", "Formalize Australian Aboriginal kinship systems (section and subsection systems) as finite groups acting on person-sets. Prove that the 4-section system is isomorphic to Z2 x Z2 and the 8-subsection system to Z2 x Z2 x Z2. Show that marriage rules correspond to coset restrictions and that the entire system forms a consistent group-theoretic structure.", ["Novelty", "Algebra", "Bridges"], 0.80),
        _sd("Infinite Games Against Death: Immortality Strategies", "Formalize a game where one player (Mortal) has finite computation and the other (Eternity) has transfinite computation. Prove that Mortal can always force at least omega rounds before losing, and that with bounded nondeterminism, Mortal can force omega-squared rounds. Connect to Infinite Time Turing Machines.", ["Novelty", "Logic", "Computation"], 0.82),
        _sd("The Mega-Sphere: All Dimensions at Once", "Construct a single algebraic object whose projections give S^0, S^1, S^2, ... simultaneously. Prove it exists as an inverse limit in the category of spheres. Show that its homology groups encode the Bernoulli numbers and that its cohomology ring is the polynomial ring on Stiefel-Whitney classes.", ["Novelty", "Geometry", "Topology"], 0.83),
        _sd("The Oracle's Burden: How Much Knowledge Is Too Much?", "Prove that adding an oracle for the halting problem to PA yields a theory that proves its own consistency but cannot decide its own soundness. Formalize the hierarchy: PA < PA^H < PA^{H^H} < ... and prove that each jump genuinely increases theorem-proving power. Show that the oracle hierarchy is isomorphic to the Turing jump hierarchy.", ["Novelty", "Logic", "Computation"], 0.88),
        _sd("Causal Loops in Category Theory: When Composition Loops Back", "Construct a category where composition is not associative but satisfies a controlled failure: (f circ g) circ h and f circ (g circ h) are naturally isomorphic but not equal. Prove that such almost-categories are exactly the bicategories and that every coherent loop-tolerant algebraic structure forms a higher category.", ["Novelty", "Algebra", "Bridges"], 0.85),

        # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
        # Wave 6: Underrepresented domain seeds (Bridges, Cryptography, Physics, Tropical)
        # ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

        # --- Bridges ---
        _sd("Homotopy Type Theory to HoTT Bridge: Univalent Foundations for Proof Transfer", "Prove that the univalence axiom enables automated proof transfer between isomorphic structures. Construct a formal pipeline: given an isomorphism f: A ≅ B and a theorem about A, mechanically produce the corresponding theorem about B. Quantify the proof compression ratio.", ["Bridges", "Logic"], 0.89),
        _sd("Information-Geometric Bridge: Fisher Metric on Statistical Manifolds", "Prove that the Fisher information metric on a statistical manifold satisfies the axioms of a Riemannian metric. Construct explicit connections between the Fisher metric and the Kullback-Leibler divergence. Bridge statistical inference to differential geometry.", ["Bridges", "Geometry"], 0.86),
        _sd("Combinatorial-Categorical Bridge: Species of Structures as Functors", "Formalize Joyal's combinatorial species as endofunctors on the category of finite sets. Prove that the exponential generating function of a species equals its analytic functor. Bridge enumerative combinatorics to category theory and analytic combinatorics.", ["Bridges", "Computation"], 0.85),
        _sd("Topological-Algebraic Bridge: Fundamental Group as a Complete Invariant", "Determine exactly which spaces are classified up to homotopy by their fundamental group. Prove that for Eilenberg-MacLane spaces K(G,1), the fundamental group is a complete invariant. Construct examples where the fundamental group fails to classify.", ["Bridges", "Algebra"], 0.83),
        _sd("Proof-Theoretic Bridge: Ordinal Analysis Across Systems", "Construct an explicit order-preserving map from the proof-theoretic ordinals of PA to those of KP set theory. Prove that epsilon_0 < psi(Omega^omega) and formalize the ordinal collapsing function psi as a term rewriting system in Lean 4.", ["Bridges", "Logic"], 0.88),
        _sd("Quantum-Classical Bridge: de Finetti Theorem for Quantum States", "Prove the quantum de Finetti theorem: symmetric quantum states on infinite tensor products are mixtures of i.i.d. states. Formalize the connection between exchangeability and independence in the quantum setting. Bridge quantum foundations to classical probability.", ["Bridges", "Physics"], 0.87),
        _sd("Logic-Physics Bridge: Consistency of Physical Theories", "Formalize the consistency of quantum field theory as a proof-theoretic question. Prove that if a physical theory T is consistent, then Con(T) is independent of PA. Show that physical consistency implies mathematical consistency but not vice versa.", ["Bridges", "Logic"], 0.84),

        # --- Cryptography ---
        _sd("Post-Quantum Lattice Cryptography: Formal Security Proofs", "Prove that the Learning With Errors (LWE) problem is as hard as worst-case lattice problems. Formalize the Regev reduction from GapSVP to LWE and prove that the resulting encryption scheme is IND-CPA secure under the LWE assumption.", ["Cryptography", "Computation"], 0.91),
        _sd("Zero-Knowledge Proof Systems: Formal Verification of Privacy", "Construct and prove correct a zero-knowledge proof system for graph 3-colorability. Prove completeness, soundness, and zero-knowledge. Formalize the simulation paradigm and show that the simulator produces indistinguishable transcripts.", ["Cryptography", "Logic"], 0.88),
        _sd("Homomorphic Encryption: Computing on Encrypted Data", "Formalize the Gentry fully homomorphic encryption scheme. Prove that the bootstrapping theorem allows unlimited computation on ciphertexts. Construct a circuit for addition and multiplication under the BGV scheme and verify correctness.", ["Cryptography", "Computation"], 0.87),
        _sd("Code-Based Cryptography: McEliece Security on the Binary Goppa Code", "Prove that distinguishing a binary Goppa code from a random linear code is NP-hard. Formalize the McEliece cryptosystem and prove IND-CPA security under the Goppa code distinguishing assumption. Analyze resistance to quantum attacks.", ["Cryptography", "Algebra"], 0.85),
        _sd("Isogeny-Based Cryptography: Supersingular Isogeny Diffie-Hellman", "Formalize the SIDH key exchange: two parties compute a shared secret from supersingular isogenies of elliptic curves. Prove that computing the isogeny from j-invariant is as hard as the quaternion isogeny path problem. Analyze the Castryck-Decru attack.", ["Cryptography", "Algebra"], 0.86),
        _sd("Secure Multi-Party Computation: Theoretical Foundations", "Prove that any polynomial-time function can be securely computed in the presence of an honest majority. Formalize the GMW compiler and prove its universal composition property. Show that malicious security adds only polynomial overhead.", ["Cryptography", "Computation"], 0.83),
        _sd("Symmetric-Key Cryptanalysis: Differential and Linear Cryptanalysis Bounds", "Prove tight upper bounds on the differential probability of an S-box. Formalize the wide-trail strategy used in AES: prove that the minimum number of active S-boxes in 4 rounds of AES is 25. Connect to the branch number of the MixColumns matrix.", ["Cryptography", "Algebra"], 0.84),

        # --- Physics ---
        _sd("Quantum Entanglement Monogamy: CKW Inequality", "Prove the Coffman-Kundu-Wootters monogamy inequality for qubit entanglement: the sum of squared concurrences is bounded by the squared concurrence with the ancilla. Formalize concurrence as an entanglement measure and extend to n-qubit systems.", ["Physics", "Computation"], 0.87),
        _sd("Hawking Radiation: Information Paradox Formalized", "Formalize the information paradox as a theorem about unitary evolution: prove that if black hole evaporation is unitary, information is preserved; if not, quantum mechanics is violated. Construct a toy model where a 2-qubit black hole evaporates unitarily and recover the initial state from radiation.", ["Physics", "Logic"], 0.90),
        _sd("Topological Order: Anyon Statistics from Ground State Degeneracy", "Prove that the ground state degeneracy of a topologically ordered system on a genus-g surface is d^g for some integer d (the quantum dimension). Formalize the connection between ground state degeneracy, anyon braiding statistics, and topological quantum field theory.", ["Physics", "Geometry"], 0.86),
        _sd("Quantum Thermodynamics: Landauer's Principle at the Nanoscale", "Prove that erasing one bit of information requires at least kT ln(2) of energy dissipation in the thermodynamic limit. Show that for finite-size systems, the bound is modified by a Jarzynski-like correction term. Formalize the connection between logical irreversibility and thermodynamic irreversibility.", ["Physics", "Computation"], 0.84),
        _sd("Chaos and the Three-Body Problem: Lyapunov Exponent Bounds", "Prove that the maximal Lyapunov exponent of the gravitational three-body problem is strictly positive, establishing deterministic chaos. Compute explicit bounds for equal-mass systems and formalize the connection between Lyapunov exponents and Kolmogorov-Sinai entropy.", ["Physics", "Geometry"], 0.85),
        _sd("Quantum Error Correction Threshold: The Eastin-Knill Theorem", "Prove the Eastin-Knill theorem: no quantum code can transversally implement a universal gate set. Formalize the threshold theorem for fault-tolerant quantum computing and prove that the threshold is approximately 1% for the surface code with depolarizing noise.", ["Physics", "Computation"], 0.88),
        _sd("Renormalization Group Flow: Wilson's Epsilon Expansion", "Formalize Wilson's epsilon expansion for the phi^4 critical exponents. Prove that eta = epsilon^2/54 + O(epsilon^3) in 4-epsilon dimensions. Verify the Feynman diagram computation and show that the renormalization group beta function has a non-trivial fixed point for d < 4.", ["Physics", "Algebra"], 0.86),

        # --- Tropical ---
        _sd("Tropical Amoebas and Ronkin Functions", "Prove that the tropical amoeba of a Laurent polynomial is the negative logarithm of its zero set. Show that the Ronkin function is convex and piecewise-linear on the amoeba complement. Connect tropical amoebas to tropical geometry via the Maslov dequantization.", ["Tropical", "Geometry"], 0.85),
        _sd("Tropical Compactification of Moduli Spaces", "Prove that the tropical compactification of the moduli space of curves M_g is a toric variety whose boundary divisors correspond to tropical curves. Formalize the connection between the Deligne-Mumford compactification and the tropical moduli space.", ["Tropical", "Geometry"], 0.87),
        _sd("Tropical Curve Counting: Gromov-Witten Invariants", "Prove that tropical curve counts equal classical Gromov-Witten invariants for toric surfaces. Formalize the correspondence theorem: each tropical curve lifts to a unique complex curve in the toric surface. Compute the tropical GW invariants for P^2.", ["Tropical", "Algebra"], 0.89),
        _sd("Tropical Scheme Theory: Groebner Bases over the Tropical Semiring", "Develop a tropical scheme theory where ideals are replaced by tropical ideals (subsemimodules of the tropical polynomial semiring closed under tropical linear combinations). Prove a tropical Buchberger algorithm exists and characterize tropical Groebner bases.", ["Tropical", "Computation"], 0.84),
        _sd("Tropical Matroid Theory: Bergman Fans and Tropical Linear Spaces", "Prove that the Bergman fan of a matroid M equals the tropical linear space of the matroid's circuit ideal. Formalize the connection between matroid connectivity and the topology of the Bergman fan. Show that nested matroids give tropical linear subspaces.", ["Tropical", "Computation"], 0.83),
        _sd("Tropical Cryptography: Min-Plus Diffie-Hellman", "Construct a Diffie-Hellman key exchange over the tropical semiring (min-plus algebra). Prove that the tropical matrix product problem is NP-hard for matrices over the min-plus semiring. Analyze security against known tropical cryptanalysis techniques.", ["Tropical", "Cryptography"], 0.82),

        # --- Emerging Areas ---
        _sd("Topological Data Analysis: Persistent Homology Stability", "Prove the stability theorem for persistent homology: the bottleneck distance between persistence diagrams is bounded by the Gromov-Hausdorff distance between the underlying spaces. Formalize the persistent homology pipeline and verify on concrete point cloud data.", ["Computation", "Geometry"], 0.88),
        _sd("Algebraic Statistics: Markov Bases for Contingency Tables", "Prove that a Markov basis for a log-linear model on contingency tables connects all fibers of the model. Formalize the Fundamental Theorem of Markov Bases and compute explicit Markov bases for the no-three-way interaction model.", ["Computation", "Algebra"], 0.84),
        _sd("Quantum Hamiltonian Complexity: QMA-Completeness of the Local Hamiltonian Problem", "Prove that the k-Local Hamiltonian Problem is QMA-complete for k >= 2. Formalize the Kitaev reduction from quantum circuit satisfiability to the local Hamiltonian problem. Analyze the promise gap and its effect on complexity.", ["Computation", "Physics"], 0.90),
        _sd("Causal Inference: Do-Calculus as Formal Logic", "Formalize Pearl's do-calculus as a formal logical system with three inference rules. Prove that do-calculus is complete for identifying causal effects in non-parametric structural equation models. Construct a decision procedure for causal effect identifiability.", ["Logic", "Computation"], 0.86),
