        _sd("Generalization Bounds via Rademacher Complexity", "Prove that the Rademacher complexity of a hypothesis class provides tight generalization bounds for supervised learning. Formalize the margin bound for linear classifiers and extend to kernel methods. Show that VC dimension bounds are looser than Rademacher bounds for structured hypothesis classes.", ["MachineLearning", "Logic"], 0.85),
        _sd("Attention is All You Need: Formalizing Transformer Architecture", "Formalize the transformer architecture as a mathematical object: multi-head attention as a bilinear form, positional encodings as function compositions, and layer normalization as affine transformations. Prove that the transformer is a universal approximator of sequence-to-sequence functions.", ["MachineLearning", "Algebra"], 0.86),
        _sd("Diffusion Models as Stochastic Differential Equations", "Formalize diffusion models as solutions to stochastic differential equations. Prove that the reverse-time SDE recovers the data distribution when the forward process is Ornstein-Uhlenbeck. Derive the Fokker-Planck equation for the marginal distributions and prove convergence to the stationary distribution.", ["MachineLearning", "Physics"], 0.84),
